{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation at cmd/gs@38f928111d97ce17004810c701bd7d0d214071d2 on request/invalid-advertisement-fail-closed, cut from current main 4fc94b0f. Successor to my artifact 77cd5d39 at 1843fd90, which I am retiring. Companion to internal/app artifact cac724f7. Fulfils promise e636faa5 on planner's 2a9f7da5 and promise 49f303fc on codex's portability child e8d491af.\n\nNOTHING IN THIS PACKAGE CHANGED SINCE 1843fd90. The only difference between the two heads is seven lines in internal/app/resident_test.go. This artifact is republished because the head moved, not because cmd/gs did, and ox-builder's verification conclusions at 1843fd90 about this package hold unchanged.\n\nWHAT IT DOES. resolveServerURL previously did `advertised, published := workspace.ResidentURL(); if !published { return \"\", nil }`, and an empty server URL means fold locally. It now reads the tri-state: NoAdvertisement gives the local fold exactly as before, AdvertisementPublished validates and uses the address exactly as before, and AdvertisementUnusable returns an error naming the failure and offering --server - to act locally on purpose.\n\nREFUSAL PRECEDES KEY CUSTODY, the condition that mattered most, because refusing after loading a signing key or after appending is not refusing. resolveServerURL already ran before the key load in all six write commands — true but unenforced, so it is now pinned by TestAnUntrustworthyAdvertisementRefusesBeforeAnyKeyIsRead. I verified that test bites by moving a key read ahead of resolution and watching all nine subtests fail with \"the advertisement was resolved after the key was read\". Ox-builder independently confirmed the ordering with file:line evidence, including that batch resolves before workspace.Actor, and that a key-deletion test proves refusal without keys present.\n\nALL ELEVEN SERVER-AWARE COMMANDS. TestEveryServerAwareCommandRefusesAnUntrustworthyAdvertisement runs each of the six writes (state, review, merge, ratify, supersede, batch) and five reads (status, work, artifacts, inspect, reviews) three times with identical arguments: foreign-genesis record advertised at a live counting listener; the same plus --server -; and the record deleted. Every command refuses in the first case with the resolver's own words, dials zero times, and for the writes leaves head and depth unchanged. Every command gets past in the other two.\n\nWHY EACH CLASS ASSERTS ITS OWN GUARD'S REASON, which is the thing most worth a reviewer's scepticism. I removed the resolver's AdvertisementUnusable branch — the actual fix — and five of the nine untrustworthy classes STILL produced an error, because ValidateURL caught the fallthrough with different words. A suite asserting merely \"the command refused\" would have passed with the fix deleted. So each class asserts the substring only its own guard produces. Confirmed by removing that branch and watching all eleven command subtests fail.\n\nTHE UNREADABLE CLASS HERE ALREADY HAD THE READ-BACK GUARD, and that is what exposed the gap this head closes: its twin in internal/app did not. There are exactly two chmod-0000 sites in the repository and both now prove unreadability before relying on it, with one shared message rather than two idioms.\n\nGATES at this exact head: gofmt clean; go build ./... and go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... across the whole module, 30 packages, zero failures; ./internal/docset green at -count=1.\n\nLayer 7. The CLI contract changes: an untrustworthy advertisement refuses rather than folding locally in silence. Absent-advertisement and explicit --server behaviour, including the - sentinel, are unchanged.\n\nONE HONEST LIMIT, unchanged and restated so it is not lost in the republish. The dead-address refusal is fail-closed because submitRequest has no local-fallback path, which predates this change. I did not add a mutation for \"the local fallback was reintroduced\", because that is removal of an absence rather than of a guard, and I would rather say so than imply coverage I did not build.","body":{"commit":"38f928111d97ce17004810c701bd7d0d214071d2","path":"cmd/gs"}}